  "description": "<p>From Chris Colvard at <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo-exts/fcrepo-upgrade-utils/pull/63\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo-exts/fcrepo-upgrade-utils/pull/63</a> </p>\n\n<blockquote><p>When migrating my fedora repository I saw that <tt>ebucore:filename</tt> statements were being dropped from my non-binary resources. I realized that my application has been using a predicate that fedora 6 is now treating as server managed for binary resources. This PR only treats the binary properties as server managed when they appear in fcr:metadata resources attached to binary resources. This allows my migration to succeed without negatively affecting binary resources.</p></blockquote>",
